ts directly on the paper. From the GitHub repo:\n- `python scripts/humanize_cn.py text.txt -o clean.txt`\n- `python scripts/academic_cn.py paper.txt -o clean.txt --compare`\n\nBut wait, the humanize-chinese project needs to be downloaded. Let me check if it's available or if I can download it.\n\nActually, looking at the search results more carefully, the humanize-chinese project claims:\n- 20+ detection categories\n- Weighted 0-100 scoring\n- Academic mode specifically for CNKI/VIP/Wanfang\n- Pure Python, no dependencies\n\nThis is exactly what I need! Let me try to download and use it.\n\nBut will I be able to `git clone` it? Let me try.\n\nAlso, I now understand the fundamental mistake I've been making. The paid services use DEEP semantic restructuring - they don't just change the surface form of the text. They:\n1. Parse the semantic structure\n2. Identify AI-typical semantic patterns (like the \"定义→举例→总结\" pattern)\n3. Restructure with different semantic patterns\n4. Then do surface-level adjustments\n\nWhat I was doing was only surface-level adjustments (词级替换、句长变化) without touching the deep semantic structure. That's why it failed.\n\nLet me try to use the humanize-chinese tool first, and if not available, try the deep semantic restructuring approach with what I have.\n\nActually, I should also look at the specific academic mode of humanize-chinese - it has 122 academic replacements and HC3-calibrated statistical analysis.\n\nLet me try to download and run humanize-chinese on the paper."}
