{"role":"assistant","content":"又翻车了。原因我已经能看出来——**「废话字注入」的思路是对的，但我的实现手法太糙了**：\n\n| 版 | 做了什么 | 结果 | 原因 |\n|:--:|---------|:----:|------|\n| v4-2 | humanize-chinese的**精心筛选的**120+学术+200通用规则 | 16% | 规则经过长期验证 |\n| 废话版 | 我自己写的**粗糙regex**加\"了\"/\"的\"/改句号为分号 | **96%** | 创造的规律太机械，检测器一秒认出 |\n\n问题是：**humanize-chinese那300多条规则是有人花几个月调试出来的。我一个regex写下去加的\"了\"和\"的\"位置不对、频率不对，反而制造了新的AI指纹。**\n\n返回到实测最好的结果——v4-2的16%。能达到的极限大概就是这个数了。\n\n如果你要继续硬碰硬，唯一还没试过的路子是 **回译（中→英→中）**，但要调用翻译API，我目前的环境做不到。\n\n如果你要的是**能过检测**的结果——路径很清楚：你写2000-3000字核心内容给我，我用v4那套确定性子替换改到10%以下。任何声称能\"纯AI生成→0%检测率\"的，要么在吹牛，要么是用了你没看到的资源（翻译API、多模型协同、自有检测器做反馈循环）。","reasoning_content":"96% AI detection rate. The \"废话字\" technique actually made things MUCH worse (from 22% → 16% → now 96%). This is a massive failure.\n\nLet me think about why:\n\n1. The \"废话字\" injection was done with regex patterns - this creates a very artificial, mechanical pattern of adding \"了\" and \"的\" in specific positions. The detector can easily recognize this as an AI pattern.\n\n2. The \"句号→分号/逗号\" replacement created unnatural comma splices.\n\n3. The real lesson: **deterministic replacement works when it's a curated, carefully designed rule set** (like the humanize-chinese 120+ academic rules) that was built by humans analyzing actual human writing patterns. My ad-hoc regex-based \"废话字\" injection was too crude and created detectable patterns.\n\nThe original v4-1 (22%) was successful because:\n- The rules came from humanize-chinese which spent months developing and testing them\n- Each replacement was carefully vetted\n- The rules were specific, targeted replacements, not broad regex patterns\n\nMy mistake: I took a good idea (废话字注入) and implemented it poorly with broad regex patterns, creating more detectable AI fingerprints.\n\nThe lesson is concrete now: **the techniques themselves aren't magic - the implementation quality matters enormously.** The 莎普爱斯 prompt works in the hands of a human (or a well-tuned system) but can't simply be regex-ified.\n\nAt this point, the real best we got was 16% (v4-2 with the humanize-chinese rules). That's the ceiling for pure AI-generated text with deterministic replacement.\n\nI should be honest with the user about this."}
