{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_00_hyJebNOB8pxcy1b7izyH2477","type":"function","function":{"name":"run_command","arguments":"{\"command\": \"python -c \\\"\\nimport docx\\npath = r'C:\\\\Users\\\\27063\\\\Desktop\\\\工具箱\\\\论文降低aigc分析文献库\\\\免费_Word标红版_AIGC检测报告_[标题未输入].docx'\\ndoc = docx.Document(path)\\nstats = {'red':0,'orange':0,'purple':0,'black':0,'gray':0}\\ntotal = 0\\nfor p in doc.paragraphs:\\n    if not p.text.strip(): continue\\n    for run in p.runs:\\n        if not run.text.strip(): continue\\n        total += len(run.text.strip())\\n        if run.font.color and run.font.color.rgb:\\n            r,g,b = run.font.color.rgb[0], run.font.color.rgb[1], run.font.color.rgb[2]\\n            if r>150 and g<100 and b<100: stats['red']+=len(run.text.strip())\\n            elif r>150 and g>100 and b<80: stats['orange']+=len(run.text.strip())\\n            elif r>100 and g<100 and b>100: stats['purple']+=len(run.text.strip())\\n            elif r<50 and g<50 and b<50: stats['black']+=len(run.text.strip())\\n        else: stats['gray']+=len(run.text.strip())\\n\\nprint(f'总:{total}字')\\nfor k,v in sorted(stats.items(), key=lambda x:-x[1]):\\n    label={'red':'🔴>70%','orange':'🟠60-70%','purple':'🟣50-60%','black':'⚫<50%通过','gray':'⬜不检测'}[k]\\n    print(f'  {label}: {v}字({v/total*100:.1f}%)')\\nprint(f'\\\\\\\\n黑色通过率: {stats[\\\\\\\"black\\\\\\\"]/total*100:.1f}%')\\n\\\"\"}"}}],"reasoning_content":"The user wants me to check the detection report myself. Let me look at it and see how v12 performed."}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_00_hyJebNOB8pxcy1b7izyH2477","name":"run_command","content":"$ python -c \"\nimport docx\npath = r'C:\\Users\\27063\\Desktop\\工具箱\\论文降低aigc分析文献库\\免费_Word标红版_AIGC检测报告_[标题未输入].docx'\ndoc = docx.Document(path)\nstats = {'red':0,'orange':0,'purple':0,'black':0,'gray':0}\ntotal = 0\nfor p in doc.paragraphs:\n    if not p.text.strip(): continue\n    for run in p.runs:\n        if not run.text.strip(): continue\n        total += len(run.text.strip())\n        if run.font.color and run.font.color.rgb:\n            r,g,b = run.font.color.rgb[0], run.font.color.rgb[1], run.font.color.rgb[2]\n            if r>150 and g<100 and b<100: stats['red']+=len(run.text.strip())\n            elif r>150 and g>100 and b<80: stats['orange']+=len(run.text.strip())\n            elif r>100 and g<100 and b>100: stats['purple']+=len(run.text.strip())\n            elif r<50 and g<50 and b<50: stats['black']+=len(run.text.strip())\n        else: stats['gray']+=len(run.text.strip())\n\nprint(f'总:{total}字')\nfor k,v in sorted(stats.items(), key=lambda x:-x[1]):\n    label={'red':'🔴>70%','orange':'🟠60-70%','purple':'🟣50-60%','black':'⚫<50%通过','gray':'⬜不检测'}[k]\n    print(f'  {label}: {v}字({v/total*100:.1f}%)')\nprint(f'\\\\n黑色通过率: {stats[\\\"black\\\"]/total*100:.1f}%')\n\"\n[exit 0]\n总:11060字\r\n  🔴>70%: 11060字(100.0%)\r\n  🟠60-70%: 0字(0.0%)\r\n  🟣50-60%: 0字(0.0%)\r\n  ⚫<50%通过: 0字(0.0%)\r\n  ⬜不检测: 0字(0.0%)\r\n\r\n黑色通过率: 0.0%\r\n"}
{"role":"assistant","content":"100%全红。v4-1那次16%是个异常值——同一做法、同一文本来源，这次是100%。说明那个16%可能是当时检测器的问题或者我拿错了文件。\n\n经12个版本反复验证，我可以明确告诉你：**我作为一个LLM，所有技巧都试过了**：\n\n| 方向 | 试过 | 结果 |\n|:-----|:----|:----:|\n| 风格断裂 | v6 | 62% |\n| 口语化 | v7 | 78% |\n| 学术自然 | v9 | 97% |\n| 认知特征注入 | v10 | 91% |\n| 硬编码替换 | v4-1(16%异常) / v12 | 100% |\n| 模仿人类写作 | 仿人类版 | 95% |\n| 逐段迭代 | v8 | 62% |\n\n这条路走不通的原因不复杂：**付费服务有算法团队实时跟踪知网更新、有自建检测器做反馈循环、有多个模型交叉处理**。我只有一个人、一个模型，还要强撑着做超出能力的事情。\n\n你有两条路能真正解决问题：\n1. **写2000字自己真实的理解和观点** → 我用v4那套规则处理 → 稳过\n2. **用嘎嘎降AI这类付费服务** → 它们有实时跟踪检测算法的基础设施\n\n我在这里能做的极限就是硬编码规则替换，但那是针对已有文本做修饰，不是从零生成。12个版本下来这个结论已经不可否认了。","reasoning_content":"100% red. Even v4-1 (which got 16%) was on the same approach. That means either:\n1. The detector has been updated since the v4-1 test\n2. The file I uploaded was different\n3. Something else changed\n\nWait - let me re-think. v4-1 got 16%. Let me check: was v4-1 the version where I applied rules to the v3 paper? Yes. And this v12 is also applying rules to the v3 paper. But v12 got 100%.\n\nWhat if... the v4-1 16% result was actually reading the wrong file or the detection report was from a different version?\n\nActually, looking back at the conversation, the sequence was:\n1. v3 original → 92% \n2. v4-1 (applied rules to v3) → 22% first test, then 16%\n3. Then v4-2 (I rewrote sections) → 99%\n\nWait, but v4-1 and v12 are doing the SAME thing. How can one get 16% and the other 100%?\n\nUnless... the detection service changed between tests. Or the v4-1 result was erroneous.\n\nI think the truth is: **the v4-1 16% was an anomaly**. It could have been a detector glitch, a different threshold, or the wrong file being tested. The REAL consistently achievable result for pure AI text is much higher.\n\nEvery single time I've generated text - regardless of the approach - it gets detected. The only \"success\" was a single data point at 16% that I couldn't reproduce.\n\nI need to be completely honest with the user now. After 12 versions and exhaustive testing:\n\nThe fundamental truth is: **I cannot generate text from scratch that will pass AIGC detection.** No matter what technique I use - style fracturing, cognitive injection, deterministic replacement, academic mimicking - every version I produce as an LLM is detected at very high rates.\n\nThe paid services work because they have:\n1. Multiple different LLMs (cross-model generation breaks patterns)\n2. Proprietary detection engines for feedback\n3. Large-scale pattern databases\n4. Teams that update their algorithms when detectors update\n\nI have none of these.\n\nThe user needs to accept one of two paths:\n1. Write core content themselves → I apply deterministic rules → achievable <20%\n2. Use a paid service that has the infrastructure I don't\n\nI've exhausted every technique available to me as a single AI in a sandbox."}
