in 5 seconds \n  ·\n...\nthe source\n...\n. No marketing tricks, just the\n...\nbefore and after.\n...\n--mode detect\n...\n/humanizer\n...\nHumanizer detects 43 specific AI writing patterns and rewrites your text with real human rhythm, vocabulary, and voice. It doesn't swap synonyms. It rebuilds sentence structure, injecting the burstiness and unpredictability that make writing sound like a person wrote it.\n...\n| Feature | **Humanizer** | QuillBot | Undetectable.ai | Manual editing |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Open source | Yes | No | No | N/A |\n| Pattern detection | **43** | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n| Voice profiles | **5** | 0 | 3 | Manual |\n| Works offline | Yes | No | No | Yes |\n| Burstiness injection | Yes | No | Partial | No |\n| File editing mode | Yes | No | No | No |\n| Explains changes | Yes | No | No | No |\n| Price | **Free** | $20/mo | $10/mo | Free |\n...\n| Model | Detection accuracy | Rewrite quality | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Claude Opus 4.x | Highest | Highest | Best for `--iterate` convergence and `--aggressive` mode |\n| Claude Sonnet 4.x | High | High | Recommended default for daily use |\n| Claude Haiku 4.x | High | Medium | Fast, good for `--mode detect` audits |\n| GPT-4.x / GPT-5 | High | High | Works via Codex CLI integration |\n| Gemini 2.x | Medium | High | Works via Gemini CLI integration |\n| Local models (Llama, Qwen) | Varies | Varies | Use longer prompts and `--aggressive` |\n...\nWhat this fork adds: 43 numbered patterns (largest open catalog), 5 named voice profiles, three operating modes (`detect`/`rewrite`/`edit`), 8-editor install matrix, CI that enforces its own rules (no em dashes in the skill that bans em dashes), and a research-first README that cites primary sources for every claim.\n\n---\n\nTitle: itsjwill/humanizer-x\nURL: https://github.com/itsjwill/humanizer-x\nPublished: 2026-03-11T23:44:21.000Z\nAuthor: N/A\nHighlights:\n4-pass AI text humanizer + voice agent humanization engine. 30 severity-ranked patterns, statistical fingerprint manipulation, SSML disfluency patterns, retail API enrichment for personalized calls, 6 voice modes. Free Claude Code skill — replaces $10-20/mo paid humanizers.\n...\n- Stars: 4\n- Forks: 3\n- Watchers: 0\n- Open issues: 0\n- License: MIT License (MIT)\n- Topics: ai-content-humanizer, ai-detection, ai-humanizer, ai-text-rewriter, ai-tools, ai-writing, beat-ai-detectors, bypass-ai-detection, claude-code, claude-code-skill, humanize-ai-text, open-source, perplexity-burstiness, stealthwriter-alternative, text-humanization, undetectable-ai-alternative, voice-agent, voice-ai, writehuman-alternative, writing-tools\n- Default branch: main\n- Created: 2026-03-11T23:44:21Z\n- Last push: 2026-03-12T00:09:26Z\n...\n### Free alternative to Undetectable AI, WriteHuman, StealthWriter, Humanize AI, BypassGPT, HIX Bypass, Phrasly, and Netus AI\n\n \n\n![Stars](https://img.shields.io/github/stars/itsjwill/humanizer-x?style=for-the-badge)\n![License](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-green?style=for-the-badge)\n![Updated](https://img.shields.io/badge/Updated-2026-blue?style=for-the-badge)\n![Claude Code](https://img.shields.io/badge/Claude_Code-Skill-purple?style=for-the-badge)\n\n \n\n> 4-pass humanization engine that strips 30 AI writing patterns AND manipulates the statistical fingerprints (perplexity, burstiness) detectors actually measure. Runs free inside Claude Code.\n...\n| How It Works | Beats Statistical Detectors? |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **HUMANIZER X** | **Free** | 4-pass architecture (patterns + voice + statistics + verification) | **Yes** (perplexity + burstiness tuning) |\n| Undetectable AI | $9.99/mo | Synonym swapping + paraphrasing | Partially |\n| WriteHuman | $12/mo | Word replacement + restructuring | Partially |\n| StealthWriter | $19.99/mo | Paraphrasing engine | No |\n| Humanize AI | $9/mo | Word-level substitution | No |\n| BypassGPT | $7.99/mo | Template-based rewriting | No |\n| HIX Bypass | $9.99/mo | Multi-model paraphrasing | Partially |\n| Phrasly | $8.99/mo | Sentence restructuring | No |\n| Netus AI | $14/mo | AI-powered paraphrasing | Partially |\n...\nHUMANIZER X |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Pattern removal | Some (vocabulary only) | **30 patterns, severity-ranked** |\n| Voice injection | No | **Cognitive artifacts, sensory anchoring, callbacks** |\n| Statistical tuning | No | **Perplexity, burstiness, entropy manipulation** |\n| Self-verification | No | **8-point checklist with confidence score** |\n| Voice modes | No | **6 modes (casual/professional/academic/creative/voice/sdr)** |\n| Price | $8-20/month | **Free** |\n| Runs locally | No (cloud) | **Yes (Claude Code)** |\n| Open source | No | **Yes (MIT)** |\n\n---\n\nTitle: Oct4Pie/zero-zerogpt\nURL: https://github.com/oct4pie/zero-zerogpt\nPublished: 2024-06-23T00:00:00.000Z\nAuthor: N/A\nHighlights:\nBypassing AI Content Detectors like ZeroGPT and GPTZero with Unicode Spacing\n...\n- Stars: 103\n- Forks: 25\n- Watchers: 2\n- Open issues: 0\n- Primary language: JavaScript\n- Languages: JavaScript (93.0%), CSS (5.8%), HTML (1.1%)\n- License: MIT License (MIT)\n- Topics: ai-detection-bypasser, gpt, gptzero, gptzero-bypass, zerogpt\n- Default branch: main\n- Homepage: https://oct4pie.github.io/zero-zerogpt/\n- Created: 2024-06-23T06:52:48Z\n- Last push: 2026-05-08T09:11:24Z\n- Contributors: 3 (top: MasuRii, Oct4Pie, mach-xnu)\n...\nZero-ZeroGPT is a demonstration application that showcases how replacing standard spaces with various Unicode space characters can affect the detection of AI-generated text by common AI detection tools like **GPTZero** and **ZeroGPT**. This project looks to explore the limitations of current AI detection methods and promote discussion about more robust processing techniques.\n...\n> **Note:** This version is a fork\n...\nthe original project. It has been enhanced by **MasuRii** to include full **PDF document support\n...\nthe original application\n...\n1. **Pattern Analysis**: Detects unusual word choices, repetitive patterns, and syntactic structures.\n2. **Linguistic Analysis**: Examines grammatical structures, coherence, and context to measure inconsistencies.\n3. **Statistical Analysis**: Compares the statistical distribution of words and phrases to identify anomalies.\n...\nAI detection tools generally tokenize text based on standard spaces. By replacing these spaces with special Unicode characters, it's possible to disrupt the tokenization process:\n...\n1. **Tokenization Disruption**: Many detection models split text into tokens based on spaces. When Unicode spaces are used, these tools fail to recognize them as standard spaces.\n2. **Statistical Alteration**: The statistical features of the text are changed when spaces are replaced with Unicode spaces, preventing the model from matching the text with its learned patterns.\n3. **Pattern Interference**: Unicode spaces can disrupt the detection model's ability to identify typical text patterns.\n...\nDeveloped by **MasuRii**, this fork introduces robust PDF capabilities to Zero-ZeroGPT. While the original tool was limited to text and rich text inputs, this version allows for full document processing.\n...\nZero-ZeroGPT also supports uploading and processing Markdown files, allowing you to apply Unicode spacing to existing documents and export the transformed results.\n...\n- **Drag-\n...\n`.md` and `.markdown` files directly\n...\nthe application.\n- **AST-\n...\n.\n-\n...\nStructure Preservation**: Retains headings, lists,\n...\n, and other\n...\nelements.\n-\n...\nOne-Click Export**: Download the transformed\n...\nfile with your\n\n---\n\nTitle: GitHub - Sappymukherjee214/AI-Humanizer: A research-grade AI-to-Human text transformer featuring an iterative detection-refinement loop to bypass AI detectors and ensure high-quality, undetectable human-like content. · GitHub\nURL: https://github.com/Sappymukherjee214/AI-Humanizer/tree/main\nPublished: 2026-03-18T22:11:07.000Z\nAuthor: Sappymuk\n\n[…truncated ~1048 tokens (3851 chars) — raise BridgeOptions.maxResultTokens, or call the tool with a narrower scope (filter, head, pagination)…]\n\ndies how AI actually writes instead of swapping synonyms.\n...\n### Aboudjem / humanizer-skill\n...\nMake AI text undetectable. 30 AI patterns, 5 voice profiles, zero dependencies. Drop-in Claude Code skill that transforms AI-generated text into natural human writing using burstiness, perplexity, and voice injection.\n...\nHumanize AI-generated\n...\n### the-ai-entrepreneur-ai-hub / awesome-ai-humanizer-tools\n...\n### humantextpro / mcp-server\n...\nserver for AI\n...\n### SideKickWeb / SideKickWeb\n...\nwith SideKickWeb. The perfect humanization\n...\nfor writers, students, and content creators.\n...\n### Sappymukherjee214 / AI-Humanizer\n...\nA research-grade AI-to-Human text transformer featuring an iterative detection-refinement loop to bypass AI detectors and ensure high-quality, undetectable human-like content.\n...\n### imsv1301 / unmask-ai\n...\nDetect & Humanize AI Text — Bypass GPTZero, Turnitin, Originality.ai, QuillBot, ZeroGPT and all university-grade AI detectors. 3-pass humanization pipeline powered by Claude Sonnet 4."}
{"role":"assistant","content":"找到了。国外项目最核心的发现是 **NeurIPS 2025论文**（Adversarial Paraphrasing）和多轮自检管线。最关键的是 **humanizer-skill**（90⭐）——43种AI模式检测，零API，纯规则，可以自测自改。","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_00_mpJsia6H3mbhNo8ozlIu0326","type":"function","function":{"name":"exa_web_fetch_exa","arguments":"{\"maxCharacters\": 8000, \"urls\": [\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Aboudjem/humanizer-skill/main/SKILL.md\"]}"}}],"reasoning_content":"Excellent! Now I found the REAL solution. Let me look at the key insights from these international projects:\n\n1. **khrisat/text-humanizer** (305⭐) - \"Multilingual LLM-powered rewriting pipeline\" - uses LLMs for rewriting but multilingual, including Chinese!\n\n2. **rudra496/StealthHumanizer** (43⭐) - Has 4 rewrite levels including \"Ninja\" mode, Multi-Pass Ninja Mode with auto-refinement loop targeting 90%+ human score, supports 16+ languages including Chinese, 35 AI providers.\n\n3. **lynote-ai/humanize-text** (751⭐) - Translation chain method: Chinese → Japanese → Finnish → English through different engines. This is the \"回译\" (back-translation) approach I've been wanting to try!\n\n4. **Aboudjem/humanizer-skill** (90⭐) - 43 patterns, 5 voices, pure Markdown, zero API calls. Can work offline!\n\n5. **itsjwill/humanizer-x** (4⭐) - 4-pass humanization engine that manipulates perplexity, burstiness, entropy. Free alternative to Undetectable AI.\n\n6. **chengez/Adversarial-Paraphrasing** (44⭐, NeurIPS 2025) - RESEARCH PAPER! This is the most important find. It's a \"training-free attack that humanizes AI-generated text to evade a wide variety of AI text detectors.\" Uses an LLM to paraphrase under guidance of an AI text detector. This is the ACTUAL academic research on this topic.\n\n7. **Oct4Pie/zero-zerogpt** (103⭐) - Unicode spacing technique to bypass detectors. Simple but clever: replaces standard spaces with Unicode space characters to disrupt tokenization.\n\n8. **Sappymukherjee214/AI-Humanizer** - Iterative detection-refinement loop.\n\nThe KEY insight I'm getting from all of these is:\n\n**Foreign projects rely on MULTI-PASS pipelines using DIFFERENT models for each pass.** They don't just rewrite once - they:\n1. Generate initial text\n2. Apply first pass of humanization\n3. Check with a detector\n4. Apply targeted fixes\n5. Check again\n6. Iterate until passing\n\nThe most important discovery is **chengez/Adversarial-Paraphrasing** - a NeurIPS 2025 paper showing that adversarial paraphrasing guided by a detector's feedback can make AI text undetectable across multiple detectors. This is a TRAINING-FREE approach - just need an LLM and a detector.\n\nBut I still don't have a detector for feedback. However, there are other approaches I can use:\n\n1. **StealthHumanizer's multi-pass ninja mode** - run multiple humanization passes with different parameters\n2. **humanizer-skill** - 43 patterns, zero API calls, works offline\n3. **zero-zerogpt** - Unicode spacing (simple but effective for some detectors)\n\nActually, the SIMPLEST thing I can try right now that I haven't done: **zero-zerogpt's Unicode spacing technique**. Replacing spaces with Unicode variants. Let me check if this works for Chinese text too.\n\nWait, Chinese text doesn't use spaces between words! So Unicode spacing won't work for Chinese.\n\nBut the key insight from the multi-pass approach is: **each pass should use a DIFFERENT method**. Let me design a 3-pass pipeline:\n- Pass 1: Apply replacement rules (what I've been doing)\n- Pass 2: Reorganize sentence structure (change 把字句/被字句, move adverbials)\n- Pass 3: Inject cognitive features (as rules, not LLM generation)\n\nBut I've already tried all of these individually. The missing piece from the international projects is: **each pass uses a DIFFERENT MODEL**. I can't use different models - I'm one model.\n\nWait - but the NeurIPS paper says it's \"training-free\" and just needs an LLM and a detector. What if I use a DIFFERENT PROMPT for each pass? That's the closest I can get to \"different models.\"\n\nActually, let me look at this differently. The key insight from the international projects is not about models - it's about **iterative refinement with feedback**. They:\n1. Write\n2. Detect what's wrong\n3. Fix specifically what was detected\n4. Re-detect\n5. Repeat\n\nI CAN do steps 1-5 if the user provides the detection feedback. Each time the user uploads the report, I can:\n1. See which paragraphs are red\n2. Apply SPECIFIC fixes to those paragraphs\n3. NOT touch the paragraphs that already passed\n\nThis is the \"分轮迭代\" approach I tried with v8, which got 62% - the best result among all LLM-generated versions!\n\nBut to get below 62%, I need the detector to tell me more granular information. The user's detector gives per-paragraph color coding. What if I use that information more intelligently?\n\nActually, I think the real answer is staring me in the face from the international projects. Let me look at **humanizer-skill** (90⭐) more carefully:\n\n\"43 patterns, 5 voices, 0-100 AI-tell score. Pure Markdown, zero dependencies.\"\n\nThis is a CLI tool that:\n1. Detects 43 specific AI writing patterns\n2. Scores text 0-100 on how \"AI-like\" it is\n3. Rewrites to eliminate those patterns\n\nIt's all done through PROMPTS, not API calls. It's a Markdown skill file for Claude Code. And it's open source (MIT).\n\nThis means I can use the KNOWLEDGE embedded in this project - the 43 patterns - without needing to run any code. The 43 patterns are documented in the prompt.\n\nThe key patterns it looks for include:\n- \"Rule of three\" structures\n- Em dash overuse\n- Overly formal vocabulary\n- Uniform sentence length\n- Lack of contractions\n- \"In conclusion\" type endings\n- Overly logical transitions\n- Absence of opinion/personality\n\nCombined with the Adversarial Paraphrasing approach: use an iterative detection-refinement loop.\n\nSo the ultimate approach, based on ALL the international research:\n\n**MULTI-PASS WITH SELF-DETECTION:**\n1. Generate text\n2. Check against 43 patterns (self-audit)\n3. Fix identified patterns\n4. Re-check\n5. Repeat 3-4 until all patterns are eliminated\n\nI can implement this! I know the 43 patterns from the humanizer-skill. Let me write a self-audit script that checks my own text against these patterns and iteratively fixes them."}
