{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_00_B6CEuDXk01nzc4ijUbXF5397","type":"function","function":{"name":"run_command","arguments":"{\"command\": \"python -c \\\"\\nimport docx\\npath = r'C:\\\\Users\\\\27063\\\\Desktop\\\\工具箱\\\\论文降低aigc分析文献库\\\\免费_Word标红版_AIGC检测报告_[v21_aigc-deslop规则版].docx'\\ndoc = docx.Document(path)\\nstats = {'red':0,'orange':0,'purple':0,'black':0}; total=0\\nfor p in doc.paragraphs:\\n    if not p.text.strip(): continue\\n    for run in p.runs:\\n        if not run.text.strip(): continue\\n        total += len(run.text.strip())\\n        if run.font.color and run.font.color.rgb:\\n            r,g,b = run.font.color.rgb[0], run.font.color.rgb[1], run.font.color.rgb[2]\\n            if r>150 and g<100 and b<100: stats['red']+=len(run.text.strip())\\n            elif r>150 and g>100 and b<80: stats['orange']+=len(run.text.strip())\\n            elif r>100 and g<100 and b>100: stats['purple']+=len(run.text.strip())\\n            elif r<50 and g<50 and b<50: stats['black']+=len(run.text.strip())\\nfor k,v in sorted(stats.items(), key=lambda x:-x[1]):\\n    label={'red':'🔴>70%','orange':'🟠60-70%','purple':'🟣50-60%','black':'⚫<50%'}[k]\\n    pct = v/total*100 if total else 0\\n    print(f'{label}: {v}字({pct:.1f}%)')\\nif total: print(f'通过率: {stats[\\\\\\\"black\\\\\\\"]/total*100:.1f}%')\\n\\\"\"}"}}],"reasoning_content":"The user has tested v21 and is showing me the detection report filename. Let me read it."}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_00_B6CEuDXk01nzc4ijUbXF5397","name":"run_command","content":"$ python -c \"\nimport docx\npath = r'C:\\Users\\27063\\Desktop\\工具箱\\论文降低aigc分析文献库\\免费_Word标红版_AIGC检测报告_[v21_aigc-deslop规则版].docx'\ndoc = docx.Document(path)\nstats = {'red':0,'orange':0,'purple':0,'black':0}; total=0\nfor p in doc.paragraphs:\n    if not p.text.strip(): continue\n    for run in p.runs:\n        if not run.text.strip(): continue\n        total += len(run.text.strip())\n        if run.font.color and run.font.color.rgb:\n            r,g,b = run.font.color.rgb[0], run.font.color.rgb[1], run.font.color.rgb[2]\n            if r>150 and g<100 and b<100: stats['red']+=len(run.text.strip())\n            elif r>150 and g>100 and b<80: stats['orange']+=len(run.text.strip())\n            elif r>100 and g<100 and b>100: stats['purple']+=len(run.text.strip())\n            elif r<50 and g<50 and b<50: stats['black']+=len(run.text.strip())\nfor k,v in sorted(stats.items(), key=lambda x:-x[1]):\n    label={'red':'🔴>70%','orange':'🟠60-70%','purple':'🟣50-60%','black':'⚫<50%'}[k]\n    pct = v/total*100 if total else 0\n    print(f'{label}: {v}字({pct:.1f}%)')\nif total: print(f'通过率: {stats[\\\"black\\\"]/total*100:.1f}%')\n\"\n[exit 0]\n🔴>70%: 9635字(88.0%)\r\n⚫<50%: 767字(7.0%)\r\n🟠60-70%: 543字(5.0%)\r\n🟣50-60%: 0字(0.0%)\r\n通过率: 7.0%\r\n"}
{"role":"assistant","content":"**有进步！** 7%黑色通过。aigc-deslop规则版是自v4-1以来最好的结果。但88%还是红的。\n\naigc-deslop的方法论里有一条**第零步**——问用户要2-3个真实研究细节。它的说明写得很直白：\n\n> \"没有真实细节我也能改写，但AI率上限只能降到20-30%，无法稳过10%。\"\n\n你那篇论文里有没有什么真实经历？比如：\n1. 写这篇论文时查阅过什么让你印象深刻的资料？\n2. 有没有哪个观点是你自己比较有看法的？\n3. 你翻文献时有没有什么发现？\n\n哪怕一句话，我嵌入到对应段落里，就能继续往下压。否则纯规则到这基本就是极限了。","reasoning_content":"Progress! 7% black (passing)! And 88% red (down from 100%). This is the BEST result since the anomalous v4-1 16% result!\n\nThe aigc-deslop rules actually made a difference - 7% passed, and the red dropped from 100% to 88%. This is REAL progress.\n\nBut 7% passing is still way too low. The key thing aigc-deslop did that I haven't done is:\n1. **The \"第零步\"**: Ask the user for 2-3 real research details\n2. **Iterative refinement**: Test → fix remaining red segments → re-test → repeat\n\nThe user has shown that they won't provide research details. But I CAN:\n1. Apply MORE aggressive aigc-deslop rules\n2. Target the specific segments that are still red\n3. Iterate\n\nBut wait - the user said \"学习人家的做法\" - learn from how they do it. aigc-deslop's methodology says: first ask the user for details, THEN rewrite. The SKILL.md says explicitly \"如果用户拒绝提供，明确告知预期：没有真实细节我也能改写，但AI率上限只能降到20-30%，无法稳过10%。\"\n\nSo I got 7% black with just rules. The remaining 88% red needs the user's real research details to go below 10% overall.\n\nLet me present this data and be honest about what's needed next."}
