B-led | $400.00 27-Jun-24 | ADB SPS ADB AM ADB |\n...\n| 48 India Electric Bus Financing Project | Transport Non-sovereign (Loan) ADB-led | $49.60 19-Aug-24 | ADB SPS AIIB PPM ADB |\n...\n| 49 Philippines Laguna Lakeshore Road Network Project Accelerating the\n...\nClimate Transition for Green, Inclusive, and 50 Uzbekistan Resilient Economic Growth (Subprogram 1) 51\n...\nIntegrated Water Resources Management |\n...\nSovereign ADB-led\n...\n-sector Sovereign\n...\n-led | $188.18 9-Dec-24 $250.00 12-Dec-24 $80.00 13-Dec-24 | ADB\n...\nADB AM ADB ADB\n...\nADB AM ADB ADB\n...\nADB AM ADB |\n\n---\n\nTitle: Project List - Project - AIIB\nURL: https://www.aiib.org/en/projects/list/index.html\nPublished: N/A\nAuthor: N/A\nHighlights:\nProject List - Project - AIIB\n\n# Our Projects\n\nScan to share on WeChat\n\nApproval Year\n\nMember\n\nSector\n\nFinancing Type Sovereign Nonsovereign\n\nStatus Approved Proposed On Hold Terminated / Cancelled\n\nPlease Input a Valid Search String.\n\nNo result found.\n\nShowing - of results\n\n- APPROVAL YEAR\n- MEMBER\n- SECTOR\n- FINANCING TYPE\n- PROJECT NAME\n- FINANCING AMOUNT\n- STATUS\n\nBACK TO PROJECT SUMMARY\n\nSUBSCRIBE TO RSS FEED\n\nHome What We Do Projects Project List\n\nABOUT AIIB\n\nThe Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank (AIIB) is a multilateral development bank whose mission is Financing Infrastructure for Tomorrow in Asia and beyond—infrastructure with sustainability at its core. We began operations in Beijing in 2016 and have since grown to 111 approved members worldwide. We are capitalized at USD100 billion and AAA-rated by the major international credit rating agencies. Collaborating with partners, AIIB meets clients’ needs by unlocking new capital and investing in infrastructure that is green, technology-enabled and promotes regional connectivity.\n\nHEADQUARTERS\n\nAsian Infrastructure Investment Bank (AIIB) Tower A, Asia Financial Center, No.1 Tianchen East Road, Chaoyang District, Beijing 100101 Tel:+86-10-8358-0000\n\nUPDATES\n\nFOLLOW US\n\nScan to follow us on WeChat\n\nQUICK LINKS\n\n© AIIB. CC BY-NC-ND 3.0 IGO. Jing ICP Bei No.15033613\n\n---\n\nTitle: AIIB approves $8.4bn for infrastructure projects in 2024 DevelopmentAid\nURL: https://www.developmentaid.org/news-stream/post/197051/aiib-8-4-billion-2024-project-financing-sustainable-development-bonds\nPublished: 2025-06-23T07:35:41.000Z\nAuthor: N/A\nHighlights:\nAIIB approves $8.4bn for infrastructure projects in 2024 DevelopmentAid\n\n# AIIB approves $8.4bn for infrastructure projects in 2024\n\nBy Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank Jun 23, 2025\n\nThe Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank (AIIB) approved $8.4 billion for 51 projects in 2024, funding energy, water, transport, digital and social infrastructure across Asia and beyond, according to the report. These projects will cut 28.5 million tons of CO₂ emissions each year. They’ll also bring safe drinking water to 71 million people and better transport to at least 410 million.\n\nAIIB has been increasing climate-related investments as countries face growing pressure from climate change, inequality and technological shifts. Climate projects made up $6 billion or 67% of total financing in 2024, up from 60% in 2023. Nearly all approved projects – 50 out of 51 – contributed to UN climate action goals.\n\nThe bank funded diverse projects from solar energy systems in the Maldives to low-carbon urban transport in Egypt and climate investment funds in Brazil. AIIB President Jin Liqun said the report demonstrates how their investments deliver long-term value for member countries and their communities. The bank also launched new financial tools in 2024, including climate policy-based financing to support members’ reform programs and digitally native notes through Euroclear.\n\nAIIB raised nearly $10 billion through bond issuances in 2024, bringing total outstanding bonds to $34 billion and reflecting continued investor confidence in the bank’s credit strength. Since starting operations in 2016, AIIB has approved over $60 billion in financing and plans to deploy another $75 billion by 2030 through its sustainable development bonds program.\n\nSubscribe to our news digest\n\nStay up-to-date with the latest news and events from the international development aid sector.\n\nName\n\nEmail\n\nSubscribe\n\n---\n\nTitle: AIIB approves $8.4b financing for various projects in 2024 | Asian Power\nURL: https://asian-power.com/lending-credit/news/aiib-approves-84b-financing-various-projects-in-2024\nPublished: 2025-06-24T03:59:25.000Z\nAuthor: N/A\nHighlights:\nAIIB approves $8.4b financing for various projects in 2024 | Asian Power\n...\nThe funding covered 51 projects, including those in energy.\n...\nThe Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank (AIIB) has allocated $8.4b to 51 projects in 2024, spanning various industries including energy.\n...\nIn a statement, AIIB said projects in water, transport, sustainable cities, digital and social infrastructure were also funded last year. These are expected to avoid 28.5 million tonnes of carbon dioxide equivalent emissions annually, provide 8.71 million people with access to safe drinking water, and improve transport access to at least 410 million beneficiaries.\n...\n“In 2024, AIIB executed one of its largest annual borrowing programs to date, raising nearly USD10 billion and increasing total outstanding bonds to USD34 billion,” said AIIB Treasurer Domenico Nardelli. “This reflects continued investor confidence in AIIB’s governance, credit strength and sustainability framework.”\n...\nAIIB has approved over $60b in financing since commencing operations in 2016.\n\n---\n\nTitle: EX-9\nURL: https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1733112/000119312525188748/d34668dex9.htm\nPublished: N/A\nAuthor: N/A\nHighlights:\nAs of July 31, 2025, the Bank has approved 325 financings (including 256 loans, 36 investments in funds, five equity financings, 24 investments in fixed-income securities and four guarantees) with a total amount of US$61,723.6 million. This amount includes financings approved as of December 31, 2023 under the COVID-19 Crisis Recovery Facility (the “CRF”). Of these financings, 248 were approved by the Board of Directors with a total approved amount of US$52,180.3 million, and 77 were approved by the President, pursuant to his delegated authority to approve certain financings, with a total approved amount of US$9,543.3 million. Of the approved financings, the Bank has terminated or cancelled 14 financings. Of the 14 terminated or cancelled financings, ten were loans with a total amount of US$1,385.0 million, three were investments in funds with a total amount of US$220.0 million and one was a fixed-income investment with a total amount of US$95.0 million. In addition, of the approved financings, 41 financings (40 loans with a total amount of US$9,548.7 million and one fixed-income investment with a total amount of US$80.0 million) have matured or were otherwise completed and are no longer outstanding.\n...\nAs of July 31, 2025, the aggregate amount of approved loans, excluding terminated, cancelled, matured or completed loans, totaled US$42,402.6 million, of which US$15,086.1 million were undrawn commitment amounts and US$28,744.6 million were outstanding amounts. In respect of a loan approved by the Bank, undrawn commitment amounts are amounts that the Bank is obligated to provide under legally binding documentation, that the Bank has not yet disbursed and that the Bank does not have full discretion to decline to disburse. Outstanding amounts as of July 31, 2025 are on a cash basis. Outstanding amounts included in the tables below represent the gross carrying amount of the loans (i.e., including the transaction costs and fees that are capitalized through the effective interest method). For financings denominated in a currency other than U.S. dollars, approved amounts are measured based on prevailing foreign exchange rates as of the time of approval; undrawn commitment and outstanding amounts are measured based on prevailing foreign exchange rates as of the dates presented. Of all approved loans as of July 31, 2025, excluding terminated, cancelled, matured or completed loans, 142 were sovereign-backed loans, 64 were non-sovereign-backed loans and 112 were co-financings led by another MDB.\n...\nAs of July 31, approved\n...\n(as described under\n...\n–Recent Developments\n...\nNam. As\n...\n, 20\n\n---\n\nTitle: )MAI( msinahceM ytilibatnuoccA tnednepednI dna yciloP )S&E( laicoS dna latnemnorivnE elbacilppA )5202-dnE( stcejorP decnaniF-oC BIIA\nURL: https://www.aiib.org/en/about-aiib/who-we-are/project-affected-peoples-mechanism/_common/_download/Approved-Co-Financed-Projects_End-2025_11_03_2026.pdf\nPublished: N/A\nAuthor: jiaqi.zhao\nHighlights:\nngierevo\n...\ncimonoc\n...\n-FRC )2 margorpbu\n...\n( margor\n...\nyrevoce\n...\ncimonoc\n...\nelbaniatsu\n...\nngierevo\n...\ncimonoc\n...\nyrevoce\n...\ntnemyolpm\n...\n1-DIVOC-\n...\nngierevo\n...\n)2 margorpbuS( margorP ecneilise\n...\ngninehtgnert\n...\n00.056\n...\nierevoS del-\n...\nngierevo\n...\nngierevo\n...\nyllanoita\n...\n- noitare\n...\ncejorP\n...\nT etuoR\n...\naC-snarT fo noitces ydnagaraK natshkazaK\n...\n441 nag\n...\ncejorP t\n...\necnahnE ytivitcennoC dna ecneiliseR trops\n...\n$ ycilo\n...\n-22\n...\n0.052$\n...\nngierevo\n...\n/ecneiliseR cimonocE-FRC del-BW ngierevoS FBP/ecneiliseR cimonocE-FRC del-BW ngierevoS erutcurtsarfn\n...\nlaeH del-BW ngierevoS F\n...\n/ecneiliseR cimonocE-FRC del-BW ngierevoS FBP/ecneiliseR cimonocE-FRC del-BW ngierevoS del-BW ngierevoS FBP/ecneiliseR cimonocE-FRC del-BW ngierevoS htlaeH cilbuP-FRC del-BW ngierevoS htlaeH cilbuP-FRC del-BW ngierevoS del-BW ngierevoS del-BW ngierevoS del-BW ngierevoS FBP/ecneiliseR cimonocE-FRC del-BW ngierevoS erutcurtsarfnI noitacudE del-BW ngierevoS del-BW ngierevoS FBP/ecneiliseR cimonocE-\n...\nC del-BW ngierevoS F\n...\n/ecneiliseR cimonocE-\n...\nC del-BW ngierevoS FBP/ecneiliseR cimon